"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThe work intended to proceed as a thriller of a brain fight with an intelligent criminal at the beginning, but moves into the realm of unpredictable comedy.  \n\nThe miscasting of a clumsy, ordinary, lethargic middle-aged researcher who took on all responsibility is used as a device for comic tension in a potentially boring case.  \n\nHis clumsy and poor suspicious behavior invites suspicion from surrounding characters and constantly brings about unintended crises.  \nIn such a situation, he accidentally meets two capable helpers and solves the case.  \n\nThe hollow ending, which ended as a simple happening, seems to be a device that completes the  that penetrates the entire work."